# Technology Stack Specification

## Project Overview

**Swift Debugging Framework MCP Server** - A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server providing AI-accessible Swift debugging strategies to modern IDEs with agentic workflows.

## Core Technology Stack

### Runtime Environment
- **Python**: 3.11+ (primary language)
- **MCP Protocol**: 1.0.0+ (Model Context Protocol compliance)
- **Async Runtime**: anyio 4.0.0+ (async support)

### Web Framework & Protocols
- **MCP Transport**: stdio/websocket modes
- **HTTP Client**: httpx 0.25.0+ (webhooks and API calls)
- **WebSocket**: Built-in MCP protocol support

### Data & Storage
- **Configuration**: PyYAML 6.0+ (YAML configuration management)
- **Data Validation**: Pydantic 2.5.0+ (type validation and serialization)
- **Search Engine**: Whoosh 2.7.0+ (full-text search with relevance scoring)
- **Git Operations**: GitPython 3.1.0+ (repository management)

### Template & Content Processing
- **Template Engine**: Jinja2 3.1.0+ (strategy template rendering)
- **Markdown Processing**:
  - python-frontmatter 1.0.0+ (YAML frontmatter parsing)
  - markdown 3.5.0+ (markdown to HTML conversion)

### Development & Quality Tools
- **Testing**: pytest 7.4.0+ with asyncio, coverage, and mocking
- **Code Quality**: black, isort, flake8, mypy
- **Pre-commit**: pre-commit 3.5.0+ (git hooks)
- **Documentation**: mkdocs with material theme

### Deployment & Monitoring
- **Containerization**: Docker with multi-stage builds
- **Process Management**: gunicorn 21.2.0+ (production deployment)
- **Logging**: structlog 23.2.0+ (structured logging)
- **Monitoring**: prometheus-client, OpenTelemetry (optional)

## Architecture Patterns

### MCP Server Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[IDE/Agent] -->|MCP Protocol| B[MCP Server]
    B --> C[Strategy Repository]
    B --> D[Search Engine]
    B --> E[Template Engine]

    C --> F[Git Repository]
    D --> G[Whoosh Index]
    E --> H[Jinja2 Templates]

    B --> I[Configuration]
    I --> J[YAML Config]
    I --> K[Environment Variables]
```

### Strategy Processing Pipeline

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Git Repository] --> B[Strategy Files]
    B --> C[Frontmatter Parser]
    C --> D[Markdown Processor]
    D --> E[Search Indexer]
    E --> F[MCP Tool Response]
```

### Data Flow Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Strategy Request] --> B[MCP Tool Handler]
    B --> C{Request Type}

    C -->|get_strategy| D[Direct Lookup]
    C -->|search_strategies| E[Search Engine]
    C -->|list_strategies| F[Category Filter]

    D --> G[Strategy Formatter]
    E --> G
    F --> G

    G --> H[Template Renderer]
    H --> I[MCP Response]
```

## Development Standards

### Code Organization
- **Package Structure**: `src/swift_debugging_mcp_server/`
- **Configuration**: `src/swift_debugging_mcp_server/config/`
- **Templates**: `src/swift_debugging_mcp_server/templates/`
- **Tests**: `tests/` (parallel structure to src)

### Quality Requirements
- **Test Coverage**: Minimum 90% (pytest-cov)
- **Type Checking**: Full mypy compliance
- **Code Formatting**: black + isort
- **Linting**: flake8 compliance
- **Documentation**: mkdocs for user documentation

### Performance Targets
- **Response Time**: Sub-100ms for strategy retrieval
- **Search Performance**: <50ms for full-text search
- **Memory Usage**: <100MB base memory footprint
- **Startup Time**: <2 seconds for server initialization

